From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:02:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the SID

The SID (eFuse) holds per-die data such as the thermal sensor
calibration, but the A733 device tree does not describe it. Add the
node. The block answers without a clock or reset being enabled.

Not covered: nvmem cells. They come with the devices that use them.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; sunxi-sid0 appears, and
its words at 0x44 match the fuse registers read directly.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 31d98b95d319..aaf9ebbcbc2d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -447,6 +447,14 @@ uart4: serial@2504000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		sid: efuse@3006000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-sid",
+				     "allwinner,sun50i-a64-sid";
+			reg = <0x03006000 0x1000>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		gic: interrupt-controller@3400000 {
 			compatible = "arm,gic-v3";
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
